{
  "about": "The lines the logs get. Add-ChatqLogLine (src/queue.ps1): local (Get-Date).ToString('o'), two spaces, the text and LF onto data/logs/<name> as UTF-8 without a BOM, the file first moved over <name>.1 when past 1 MB (1048576 bytes). Write-ChatqReplyLog (src/phone.ps1): each run of CR and LF one space, as 'phone: <text>' in watcher.log and as itself in replies.log. Send-ChatqAlert (src/alerts.ps1): <o> TAB <event> TAB <text> LF onto alerts.log before any channel, each run of \\s in the text one space, the event as it came. A log case runs its steps and answers every file in logs/ with its text; a roll case lays files down from a recipe (n bytes, byte i LF where i % 100 is 99, else x), adds one line, and answers each file's size and the last line of the one written to. Rust: log::add_log_line_in, write_reply_log, add_alert_line",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "line-first",
      "input": {
        "kind": "log",
        "zone": "Korea Standard Time",
        "utcOffsetMinutes": 540,
        "steps": [
          {
            "at": "2026-10-15T01:00:00Z",
            "act": "line",
            "log": "watcher.log",
            "text": "watcher 4242 started (9.8.7)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "watcher.log",
            "text": "2026-10-15T10:00:00.0000000+09:00  watcher 4242 started (9.8.7)\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
